keywords:
  - grokking
  - federated learning
  - FedAvg
  - modular arithmetic
  - mechanistic interpretability
abstract: >-
  Code, run manifests, per-run histories and analysis for a study of whether
  grokking survives federated averaging, across six model/task setups and the
  FedAvg family. Federation delays grokking rather than breaking it: memorisation
  slows with the number of clients while the memorise-to-generalise delay stays
  flat, partition structure matters more than fragmentation, and at high local
  work a quadratic MLP on S5 reaches a stable state that memorises and never
  generalises.
